xample and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new numbers. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Transfer to a new problem"}],"title":"Year 3, Week 27, Lesson 2: Measuring capacity","unit_number":7,"unit_title":"Area, capacity, volume and mass","week":27,"week_in_unit":3,"word_challenges":null,"worked_example":"WORK THROUGH THIS\nIf water sits at the 250 mL mark, capacity poured is 250 mL (for that pour). Estimate a cup then measure to compare.\n\nWrite what makes this example accurate, naming the places, values or distances used.","worked_visuals":[{"alt":"Measuring jug reading at the liquid line.","caption":"Eye level improves accuracy.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Scale</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">read at eye level</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Mark</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">250 mL line</text></g></svg>"},{"alt":"Estimate-then-measure for capacity.","caption":"Halfway between marks is a midpoint estimate.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#29